# exiftool — image metadata

> Focused on six fields: Make, Model, Description, Author, Keywords, and GPS location.
> For everything else, see the [official documentation](https://exiftool.org).

---

## Read

```sh
exiftool image.jpg                       # dump all metadata
exiftool -Make -Model image.jpg          # read specific tags
exiftool -Description image.jpg          # reads the description of the image (if present)
exiftool -s image.jpg                    # short tag names (good for scripting)
exiftool -G image.jpg                    # show which group each tag belongs to
```

### Read just the six fields

```sh
exiftool \
  -Make \
  -Model \
  -Description \
  -Artist \
  -Keywords \
  -GPSLatitude \
  -GPSLongitude \
  image.jpg
```

---

## Make and Model

```sh
# read
exiftool -Make image.jpg
exiftool -Model image.jpg

# write
exiftool -Make="Canon" image.jpg
exiftool -Model="EOS R5" image.jpg

# write both at once
exiftool -Make="Canon" -Model="EOS R5" image.jpg
```

> These live in the EXIF group. Cameras write them automatically — editing is
> mostly useful for forensic work or correcting bad metadata.

