## Description

Description lives in multiple places depending on the format and which tool wrote it.
The most portable approach is to write to both EXIF and XMP:

```sh
# read (checks common locations)
exiftool -Description image.jpg
exiftool -ImageDescription image.jpg      # EXIF variant
exiftool -XMP:Description image.jpg       # XMP variant

# write to EXIF
exiftool -ImageDescription="Sunset over the harbour" image.jpg

# write to XMP (preferred for compatibility with Lightroom, Photoshop, etc.)
exiftool -XMP:Description="Sunset over the harbour" image.jpg

# write to both at once
exiftool \
  -ImageDescription="Sunset over the harbour" \
  -XMP:Description="Sunset over the harbour" \
  image.jpg
```

