## Keywords / tags

Keywords are stored across three different fields depending on the tool that wrote them.
Writing to all three gives the broadest compatibility (Lightroom, stock platforms, etc.):

```sh
# read — try all three
exiftool -Keywords image.jpg              # IPTC
exiftool -XMP:Subject image.jpg           # XMP (used by Lightroom, Adobe)
exiftool -XMP:HierarchicalSubject image.jpg  # hierarchical keywords (Lightroom)

# add a single keyword (IPTC)
exiftool -Keywords="landscape" image.jpg

# add multiple keywords
exiftool -Keywords="landscape" -Keywords="travel" -Keywords="sunset" image.jpg

# append without overwriting existing keywords
exiftool -Keywords+="newkeyword" image.jpg

# write to IPTC and XMP together (recommended)
exiftool \
  -Keywords="landscape" \
  -Keywords="travel" \
  -XMP:Subject="landscape" \
  -XMP:Subject="travel" \
  image.jpg

# remove a specific keyword
exiftool -Keywords-="unwanted" image.jpg

# remove all keywords
exiftool -Keywords= -XMP:Subject= image.jpg
```

> **Note:** IPTC `Keywords` and XMP `Subject` are separate fields that most tools
> treat as equivalent. If only one is set, some apps won't see it.

