## GPS location

```sh
# read
exiftool -GPSLatitude -GPSLongitude image.jpg
exiftool -GPSLatitude -GPSLongitude -GPSAltitude image.jpg

# read in decimal format (instead of degrees/minutes/seconds)
exiftool -c "%.6f" -GPSLatitude -GPSLongitude image.jpg

# write — Ref tags are required to indicate N/S and E/W
exiftool \
  -GPSLatitude=51.5074 \
  -GPSLatitudeRef=N \
  -GPSLongitude=0.1278 \
  -GPSLongitudeRef=W \
  image.jpg

# write with altitude
exiftool \
  -GPSLatitude=51.5074 \
  -GPSLatitudeRef=N \
  -GPSLongitude=0.1278 \
  -GPSLongitudeRef=W \
  -GPSAltitude=42 \
  -GPSAltitudeRef=0 \
  image.jpg

# copy GPS from another file
exiftool -tagsFromFile source.jpg -GPS:all target.jpg

# strip all GPS data (privacy)
exiftool -GPS:all= image.jpg
exiftool -GPS*= image.jpg                # wildcard form
```

> **`GPSAltitudeRef`**: `0` = above sea level, `1` = below sea level.

